+# Woodstock steel-transfer lead in a draft-minutes attachment
+
+**November 4, 2026.** A preserved newspaper-hosted copy of a Woodstock municipal packet gives a concrete transfer-record target and a source-status qualification. It has not been byte-matched to a city-held original. Scope: **STL01-STL03 / B188 / H005 / AUD011 / AUD016**.
+
+## Exact source layers
+
+The [outer agenda](https://bloximages.newyork1.vip.townnews.com/tribuneledgernews.com/content/tncms/assets/v3/editorial/6/20/620dd652-4783-11e6-96e3-f328b22f6f2b/5783c7a3f216a.pdf.pdf#page=1) is dated **July 11, 2016**. Its [page 2, item 9.2](https://bloximages.newyork1.vip.townnews.com/tribuneledgernews.com/content/tncms/assets/v3/editorial/6/20/620dd652-4783-11e6-96e3-f328b22f6f2b/5783c7a3f216a.pdf.pdf#page=2) concerns approval of earlier minutes. The [staff cover at packet/physical page 201](https://bloximages.newyork1.vip.townnews.com/tribuneledgernews.com/content/tncms/assets/v3/editorial/6/20/620dd652-4783-11e6-96e3-f328b22f6f2b/5783c7a3f216a.pdf.pdf#page=201), **DOC ID 4013**, identifies the **June 13, 2016** minutes and marks their review **“Pending”** for July 11.
+
+The [attachment's first face, physical page 202](https://bloximages.newyork1.vip.townnews.com/tribuneledgernews.com/content/tncms/assets/v3/editorial/6/20/620dd652-4783-11e6-96e3-f328b22f6f2b/5783c7a3f216a.pdf.pdf#page=202), is captioned **“06132016 1st draft.”** At [physical/packet page 206, internal page 5, entry 6](https://bloximages.newyork1.vip.townnews.com/tribuneledgernews.com/content/tncms/assets/v3/editorial/6/20/620dd652-4783-11e6-96e3-f328b22f6f2b/5783c7a3f216a.pdf.pdf#page=206), the steel-transfer item bears **“[APPROVED]”**, describes Port Authority ownership transfer to Woodstock, and reports a **6-0** consent motion covering items **7.1-7.12**. Its wording refers to an attached agreement; no operative agreement was acquired as a distinct identified record in this review.
+
+Both approval labels are preserved with their subjects. Neither is treated as a controlling final legal disposition. An agenda, a proposed minutes approval and a draft's description of an earlier action are different record fields; actual later approval and signed execution remain unverified. No contradiction, correction, deception or historical explanation is selected.
+
+## Evidence strength and the next original
+
+This is a specific lead to the **June 13, 2016 transfer item**, its original agenda/attachments, final minutes and executed instrument. It is not a deed, release, item-level receipt or scientific test. The quoted transfer description does not authenticate the artifact's building, original recovery, present custody or testing access. The inspected entry supplies no artifact inventory identifier.
+
+The preservation-positive possibility is that an agreement and later custody records can document a surviving piece and conditions for its use. Contrary possibilities include an unexecuted proposal, a changed instrument or an uncertain physical match. These remain untested. Obtain the actual agreement and inventory/selection/dispatch/receipt chain before choosing between them. Woodstock is not joined to Dixon I-0094, Beverly Hills I-0137, Clearwater G-0006, Smithsonian/FBI objects or any NIST/FEMA/WTC 7 specimen.
+
+On page 206 the same consent-vote sentence occurs **six times** beneath different agenda entries. The count is reproducible from this page's text; it is not six independent witnesses, steel decisions or empirical results. Actual meeting motion count was not independently verified.
+
