+
+The captured PDF has **252 pages, 12,687,834 bytes**, SHA-256 **`c0c9d3b23f3945259a6d0f9a66c3f48308f852b160c73c15425f375754667c0a`**; acquisition completed **2026-11-05T00:38:50.443020+00:00**. Embedded creation/modification fields report **July 7, 2016**; HTTP Last-Modified reports **July 11, 2016**. These are retained as metadata, not substituted for a signature or transfer date. The mirror URL was already located in an earlier search, so this acquisition is not a first-discovery claim. One official-counterpart query returned the same mirror and unrelated results; no city-native byte equivalence is asserted.
+
+Full visible faces **1, 2, 201, 202 and 206** were read at 144 dpi. All 252 text layers were mechanically checked for three exact steel/WTC phrases and URI annotations; only page 206 matched those phrase locators. The other 247 faces were not visually read. The PDF catalog exposes no Names tree, but that does not prove no separately filed or scanned agreement exists. No whole-packet attachment completeness or global absence claim follows.
+
+Source checks matched the byte hash, page count, nine selected text locators and six repeated motion strings. These checks do not authenticate historical signatures, custody, legal effect, city-original identity or a physical mechanism. The public export contains notes, locators and code; the raw packet, rasters, unrelated records, personal names/contact information and signatures remain outside it.
